// SHOULD NOT WARN: qualified Qt module names must not trigger Microsoft.Spacing.
// TokenIgnores blanks the enumerated QtQuick/QtQml module names before rules fire.

/*!
    \page qtquick-modules.html
    \title Qt Quick Related Modules

    Qt Quick spreads its functionality across several modules. The core
    module is QtQuick. QtQuick.Layouts adds layout support. UI controls
    come from QtQuick.Controls, with the style variants
    QtQuick.Controls.Material, QtQuick.Controls.Universal,
    QtQuick.Controls.Fusion, QtQuick.Controls.Imagine, and
    QtQuick.Controls.iOS.

    Particle effects use QtQuick.Particles. Vector graphics use
    QtQuick.Shapes. Timeline-based animations use QtQuick.Timeline.
    Native dialogs use QtQuick.Dialogs. Local storage access uses
    QtQuick.LocalStorage. The virtual keyboard uses
    QtQuick.VirtualKeyboard, and its settings live in
    QtQuick.VirtualKeyboard.Settings. Scene integration uses
    QtQuick.Scene2D and QtQuick.Scene3D.

    For QML-side model types, see QtQml.Models and QtQml.XmlListModel.
    Background workers use QtQml.WorkerScript.

    Experimental APIs use the Qt.labs prefix. Examples are
    Qt.labs.qmlmodels, Qt.labs.animation, and Qt.labs.platform. Others are
    Qt.labs.folderlistmodel and Qt.labs.settings. The prefix also covers
    Qt.labs.sharedimage and Qt.labs.wavefrontmesh.

    3D rendering support uses QtQuick3D. Its post-processing effects live
    in QtQuick3D.Effects, and its particle system lives in
    QtQuick3D.Particles3D.
*/


